  "worked_solution": "We have to divide a negative number $(-36)$ by another negative number $(-7).$ So the result will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-36)÷(-7)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $36$ by $7$ without any signs: $36÷7=5\\,\\frac{1}{7}.$ Therefore, we get\n\n$$\n(-36)÷(-7)=5\\,\\frac{1}{7}.\n$$",
